.TH SUBI 1 "2026-08-31" "SUB Language" "SUB Language Manual"
.SH NAME
subi \- run a SUB program, or start the SUB REPL
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B subi
.RI [ script.sb ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B subi
interprets a SUB source file. With no argument it starts an interactive
read-eval-print loop.
.PP
.B subi
is the specification for the language: what it prints and the status it
exits with is what every compiled and transpiled backend is tested against.
When a backend disagrees with it, the backend is wrong.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SUB_PATH
A colon-separated list of directories searched by
.B import
before the bundled standard library.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/sub/stdlib
The standard library:
.IR math ", " arrays ", " strings ", " io .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The program ran to completion.
.TP
.B 1
The source did not compile.
.TP
.B 70
The program stopped on a runtime error \- division by zero, an index out of
range, an argument out of range. Every backend agrees on this status.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
subi hello.sb
subi
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sub (1),
.BR subc (1)
.SH BUGS
Report at https://github.com/subhobhai943/sub-lang/issues
